{"name":"Astrogranite Debris","hex":"#3b424c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"debris","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Rubble, wreckage, scattered remains of something destroyed.","Litter and discarded refuse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debris"}],"entries":[{"title":"Debris","blocks":[{"text":"Debris is rubble, wreckage, ruins, litter and discarded garbage/refuse/trash, scattered remains of something destroyed, or, as in geology, large rock fragments left by a melting glacier, etc. Depending on context, debris can refer to a number of different things. The first apparent use of the French word in English is in a 1701 description of the army of Prince Rupert upon its retreat from a battle with the army of Oliver Cromwell, in England."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Joplin_2011_tornado_damage.jpg/330px-Joplin_2011_tornado_damage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debris","wikidata":"Q637703"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/ObsidianDomeCA.JPG/500px-ObsidianDomeCA.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/ObsidianDomeCA.JPG/500px-ObsidianDomeCA.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Obsidian debris (talus), Obsidian Dome, California.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AObsidianDomeCA.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Marine_debris_on_Hawaiian_coast.jpg/330px-Marine_debris_on_Hawaiian_coast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Marine_debris_on_Hawaiian_coast.jpg/330px-Marine_debris_on_Hawaiian_coast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten